# Line endings: LF everywhere, in the repo AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default, and what this
# workstation has set) checks files out with CRLF while storing them as LF. The
# repo stays clean, but Prettier does not: `.prettierrc` sets no `endOfLine`, so
# it defaults to `lf` and flags every single line of every checked-out file.
# `npm run lint` on Windows reported 82,024 errors, essentially all of them
# `Delete ␍` — which makes the command useless locally, so real lint failures
# hide in the noise and nobody notices when a new file is written with CRLF.
#
# It also explains why files show as modified with an empty `git diff`: the
# working tree and the index genuinely differ, but only in line endings.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` tells git to normalise on commit (already happening) and to
# check out LF on every platform (the part that was missing). Because the stored
# objects are already LF, adding this changes no file content — it only affects
# what lands in the working tree from here on.
#
# To normalise files already checked out with CRLF, after committing this:
#     git add --renormalize .
# and commit whatever that stages (it should be nothing but line endings).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4  binary
*.webm binary
